PLAN DEVIATION (recorded in the plan body): the file map assigned this to
agui/convert.go. Not buildable — convert.go is package agui, agui imports
agui/internal/stream, so processor.go cannot import convert.go without a
cycle. Verified the import direction before deviating. Extraction lives
next to its consumers instead; agui can still reach it via the existing
stream. alias bridge if history conversion ever needs it.

ADK findings that shaped the code:
- session.Event.UnmarshalJSON nils an all-zero NodeInfo, but ONLY on the
  JSON path, and only because adk-python always writes a nodeInfo object.
  In-process events can therefore carry a non-nil NodeInfo with an empty
  Path, which is exactly the case FR1's author fallback covers. Had the
  normalisation been unconditional, that fallback would be dead code.
- Routes live on Event, not NodeInfo, so a non-workflow event can have
  Routes. Membership is decided by the NodeInfo pointer alone.

Design decisions:
- OutputPaths returns nil for a pathless node with no OutputFor rather
  than [""], so P3 cannot write _adk.nodeOutputs. with an empty key.
- modelTextOf skips Thought parts. Reasoning is not a node result, and
  including it would put chain-of-thought into client-visible state.

